// tap-echo: --buffer 65535
// Ensure that the reception of a TCP segments with the RST-ACK-bits set in the
// LISTEN state does not result in a state change and no response is sent.
// Adapted from freebsd-net/tcp-testsuite commit 04b8c73fc5081fe3792f1bed9168c9b22aaedddb,
// state-event-engine/rcv-rst-ack-listen/rcv-rst-ack-without-data-listen-ipv4.pkt
// (BSD-2-Clause; notice below). Changes for Zhida's packet-only runner, tap-echo
// being the application (fuzz/packetdrill/README.md, "Upstream suites"):
// - IPv4 variant. Dropped: sysctls, which set FreeBSD defaults; fcntl;
//   getsockopt(SO_RCVBUF); --tolerance_usecs=75000 (the runner keeps packetdrill's 4
//   ms); sockstat and tcpdrop commands except where replaced below.
// - socket/bind/listen dropped: tap-echo listens on port 8080. --buffer 65535 makes
//   Zhida's SYN-ACK window 65535, as upstream's.
// - The first segment goes at time 0 (upstream: 0.1 s after listen(); packetdrill
//   requires the first event at 0, and tap-echo listens before the script starts).
//
//
